{"title":"Career Roadmap · Resolution Professional Assistant","role":"Resolution Professional Assistant","summary":"A Resolution Professional Assistant supports insolvency professionals, resolution professionals and their teams in managing the legal, procedural, documentation and administrative aspects of insolvency and restructuring assignments.","facts":{"Current degree":"Law - LLB / BA LLB / BBA LLB / B.Com LLB / B.Sc LLB (Integrated)","Course":"Insolvency & Bankruptcy Law"},"about":[],"intro":[{"type":"flow","items":["Default","Legal Provision","Application","Creditor Position","Debtor Position","Judicial Decisions","Practical Consequence"]},{"type":"p","text":"Build a database of important insolvency cases and track:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Case name"},{"text":"Year"},{"text":"Issue"},{"text":"Statutory provision"},{"text":"Decision"},{"text":"Practical significance"}]}],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A Resolution Professional Assistant supports insolvency professionals, resolution professionals and their teams in managing the legal, procedural, documentation and administrative aspects of insolvency and restructuring assignments."},{"type":"p","text":"In India, this career sits within the Insolvency and Bankruptcy Code (IBC) ecosystem, involving stakeholders such as:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Insolvency professionals"},{"text":"Insolvency Professional Entities"},{"text":"Corporate debtors"},{"text":"Creditors"},{"text":"Committee of Creditors"},{"text":"Resolution applicants"},{"text":"Liquidators"},{"text":"Financial institutions"},{"text":"Operational creditors"},{"text":"Resolution applicants"},{"text":"Adjudicating authorities"},{"text":"Insolvency professional agencies"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Typical work can include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Legal research"},{"text":"Case documentation"},{"text":"Claims-related documentation"},{"text":"Notice preparation"},{"text":"Meeting documentation"},{"text":"Resolution-plan analysis support"},{"text":"Regulatory compliance tracking"},{"text":"Due diligence"},{"text":"Asset and liability information review"},{"text":"Stakeholder communication"},{"text":"Court/tribunal filing support"}]},{"type":"note","label":"Important","text":"A Resolution Professional Assistant is not automatically a Resolution Professional. Becoming an Insolvency Professional/Resolution Professional involves separate statutory eligibility, examination, registration and professional requirements under the applicable IBC/IBBI framework. This roadmap is for the support/associate pathway."}]},{"heading":"Career Pathway","kind":"growth","blocks":[{"type":"flow","items":["LL.B. / Integrated LL.B.","Corporate + Insolvency Law","IBC & Insolvency Procedures","Insolvency / Restructuring Internship","Legal / Insolvency Associate","Resolution Professional Assistant","Senior Insolvency Associate","Insolvency Professional Team Lead","Eligible Professional / Insolvency Professional Pathway"]},{"type":"p","text":"A law graduate can also develop toward:"},{"type":"flow","items":["LL.B.","IBC / Restructuring Team","Insolvency Associate","Resolution Professional Support","Restructuring Specialist"]}]},{"heading":"What Does a Resolution Professional Assistant Do?","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"The role is primarily a support and execution position."},{"type":"p","text":"Typical responsibilities include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Reviewing legal documents"},{"text":"Conducting IBC research"},{"text":"Preparing case summaries"},{"text":"Supporting claims verification"},{"text":"Maintaining creditor records"},{"text":"Preparing notices"},{"text":"Supporting Committee of Creditors meetings"},{"text":"Preparing meeting agendas and minutes"},{"text":"Reviewing resolution-plan documents"},{"text":"Supporting due diligence"},{"text":"Maintaining statutory timelines"},{"text":"Preparing filing documents"},{"text":"Coordinating with lawyers and professionals"},{"text":"Tracking court/NCLT proceedings"},{"text":"Maintaining case documentation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Typical workflow"},{"type":"flow","items":["Corporate Default","Insolvency Proceedings","Resolution Professional","Claims Collection","Claims Verification","Committee of Creditors","Resolution Plans","Evaluation & Voting","Approval / Further Process","Implementation / Closure"]},{"type":"p","text":"The exact process depends on the type and stage of insolvency proceeding."}]},{"heading":"Year 1 — Legal Foundations","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Legal Methods"},{"text":"Contract Law"},{"text":"Constitutional Law"},{"text":"Law of Torts"},{"text":"Legal Research"},{"text":"Legal Writing"},{"text":"Communication"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Build strong research habits"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn how to:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Read legislation"},{"text":"Identify legal issues"},{"text":"Find case law"},{"text":"Prepare case briefs"},{"text":"Summarize judgments"},{"text":"Track amendments"},{"text":"Compare statutory provisions"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 2 — Corporate & Commercial Law"},{"type":"p","text":"Develop knowledge of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Company Law"},{"text":"Contract Law"},{"text":"Commercial Law"},{"text":"Banking Law"},{"text":"Securities Law"},{"text":"Corporate Governance"},{"text":"Civil Procedure"},{"text":"Property Law"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Understand corporate distress"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn concepts such as:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Debt"},{"text":"Default"},{"text":"Secured creditors"},{"text":"Unsecured creditors"},{"text":"Corporate guarantees"},{"text":"Charges"},{"text":"Corporate restructuring"},{"text":"Financial statements"},{"text":"Corporate governance failures"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 3 — Insolvency & Bankruptcy Law"},{"type":"p","text":"This becomes the main specialization stage."},{"type":"p","text":"Study the structure of the IBC framework and the roles of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Corporate debtor"},{"text":"Financial creditor"},{"text":"Operational creditor"},{"text":"Insolvency professional"},{"text":"Resolution professional"},{"text":"Committee of Creditors"},{"text":"Resolution applicant"},{"text":"Liquidator"},{"text":"Adjudicating authority"},{"text":"Insolvency Professional Agency"},{"text":"IBBI"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Learn the difference between:"},{"type":"p","text":"Resolution and Liquidation."},{"type":"h","text":"Simplified model"},{"type":"flow","items":["Financial Distress","Insolvency Process","Resolution Attempt","Successful Resolution"]},{"type":"p","text":"│"},{"type":"p","text":"└──────────────→ Liquidation if resolution fails"}]},{"heading":"Final Year — Practical Insolvency Work","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"IBC case analysis"},{"text":"Insolvency applications"},{"text":"Claims documentation"},{"text":"Resolution plans"},{"text":"CoC processes"},{"text":"Legal notices"},{"text":"NCLT proceedings"},{"text":"Case-law research"},{"text":"Compliance calendars"},{"text":"Insolvency documentation"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Develop the ability to follow a case from:"},{"type":"flow","items":["admission","claims","CoC","resolution process","approval/other outcome"]}]},{"heading":"Core Insolvency Skill Stack","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Skill","Importance"],"rows":[[{"text":"Insolvency Law"},{"text":"⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐"}],[{"text":"IBC Framework"},{"text":"⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐"}],[{"text":"Company Law"},{"text":"⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐"}],[{"text":"Contract Law"},{"text":"⭐⭐⭐⭐"}],[{"text":"Legal Research"},{"text":"⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐"}],[{"text":"Case-Law Analysis"},{"text":"⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐"}],[{"text":"NCLT Procedures"},{"text":"⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐"}],[{"text":"Documentation"},{"text":"⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐"}],[{"text":"Claims Analysis"},{"text":"⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐"}],[{"text":"Financial Statements"},{"text":"⭐⭐⭐⭐"}],[{"text":"Due Diligence"},{"text":"⭐⭐⭐⭐"}],[{"text":"Restructuring"},{"text":"⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐"}],[{"text":"Excel"},{"text":"⭐⭐⭐⭐"}],[{"text":"Negotiation"},{"text":"⭐⭐⭐"}],[{"text":"Stakeholder Management"},{"text":"⭐⭐⭐⭐"}]]}]},{"heading":"Understanding the Insolvency Ecosystem","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A student should understand how the major participants interact."},{"type":"p","text":"IBBI"},{"type":"p","text":"│"},{"type":"p","text":"┌────────────┼────────────┐"},{"type":"p","text":"↓ ↓ ↓"},{"type":"p","text":"IPA IPs Regulations"},{"type":"flow","items":["│","Resolution Professional"]},{"type":"p","text":"│"},{"type":"p","text":"┌────────────┼────────────┐"},{"type":"p","text":"↓ ↓ ↓"},{"type":"p","text":"Creditors CoC Resolution"},{"type":"p","text":"Applicants"},{"type":"p","text":"The exact institutional and procedural structure should always be checked against the current IBC, IBBI regulations, rules and applicable NCLT/NCLAT decisions."}]},{"heading":"Claims Management","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Claims are an important practical component of insolvency assignments."},{"type":"p","text":"Learn how to support:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Claim documentation"},{"text":"Claim verification"},{"text":"Creditor classification"},{"text":"Supporting evidence"},{"text":"Claim reconciliation"},{"text":"Claim-status tracking"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Claims workflow"},{"type":"flow","items":["Claim Received","Document Verification","Amount Reconciliation","Creditor Classification","Legal / Financial Review","Record Update","Communication"]},{"type":"p","text":"A law graduate should understand the legal basis of a claim while working with financial professionals for numerical verification."}]},{"heading":"Committee of Creditors","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Understand the role of the Committee of Creditors (CoC)."},{"type":"p","text":"Learn about:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Composition"},{"text":"Voting"},{"text":"Meetings"},{"text":"Agenda"},{"text":"Minutes"},{"text":"Information provided to members"},{"text":"Resolution-plan evaluation"},{"text":"Professional advice"},{"text":"Decision documentation"}]},{"type":"p","text":"A Resolution Professional Assistant may support the preparation and documentation associated with CoC meetings."}]},{"heading":"Resolution Plans","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Develop basic understanding of how resolution plans are evaluated."},{"type":"p","text":"Study concepts such as:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Resolution applicant"},{"text":"Eligibility"},{"text":"Plan structure"},{"text":"Creditor recoveries"},{"text":"Treatment of stakeholders"},{"text":"Feasibility"},{"text":"Viability"},{"text":"Implementation"},{"text":"Compliance requirements"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Simplified process"},{"type":"flow","items":["Resolution Applicant","Resolution Plan","Eligibility Review","Commercial Evaluation","Legal Review","CoC Consideration","Voting","Approval / Rejection"]},{"type":"p","text":"The actual legal and commercial evaluation involves multiple statutory and regulatory requirements."}]},{"heading":"NCLT & NCLAT Knowledge","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Develop familiarity with:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"National Company Law Tribunal"},{"text":"National Company Law Appellate Tribunal"},{"text":"Insolvency applications"},{"text":"Orders"},{"text":"Appeals"},{"text":"Procedural filings"},{"text":"Case timelines"},{"text":"Judicial interpretation of the IBC"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Learn to prepare:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Case chronology"},{"text":"Case brief"},{"text":"Issues list"},{"text":"Relevant judgments"},{"text":"Procedural status report"}]}]},{"heading":"Insolvency Case Analysis","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Use a structured framework:"}]},{"heading":"Financial Skills","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A law graduate working in insolvency should not be limited to legal knowledge."},{"type":"p","text":"Learn basic:"},{"type":"h","text":"Accounting"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Balance sheet"},{"text":"Profit & loss statement"},{"text":"Cash-flow statement"},{"text":"Assets"},{"text":"Liabilities"},{"text":"Equity"},{"text":"Working capital"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Finance"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Debt"},{"text":"Interest"},{"text":"Security"},{"text":"Recovery"},{"text":"Valuation basics"},{"text":"Discounted cash flow concepts"},{"text":"Enterprise value"},{"text":"Liquidation value"}]},{"type":"p","text":"You do not need to become a chartered accountant, but you should be able to read and understand financial information sufficiently to support insolvency work."}]},{"heading":"Excel Skills","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Become comfortable with:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Sorting/filtering"},{"text":"XLOOKUP"},{"text":"INDEX/MATCH"},{"text":"Pivot tables"},{"text":"Conditional formatting"},{"text":"Data validation"},{"text":"Charts"},{"text":"Basic financial calculations"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Example creditor tracker"},{"type":"table","header":["Creditor","Claim","Verified","Category","Voting","Status"],"rows":[[{"text":"Creditor A"},{"text":"₹X"},{"text":"Yes"},{"text":"Financial"},{"text":"Yes"},{"text":"Verified"}],[{"text":"Creditor B"},{"text":"₹X"},{"text":"Pending"},{"text":"Operational"},{"text":"No"},{"text":"Review"}],[{"text":"Creditor C"},{"text":"₹X"},{"text":"Yes"},{"text":"Financial"},{"text":"Yes"},{"text":"Verified"}]]},{"type":"p","text":"Use fictional/sample data when building a student portfolio."}]},{"heading":"Due Diligence","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Learn to examine:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Corporate records"},{"text":"Contracts"},{"text":"Loans"},{"text":"Security interests"},{"text":"Litigation"},{"text":"Assets"},{"text":"Liabilities"},{"text":"Related-party transactions"},{"text":"Regulatory issues"},{"text":"Financial statements"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Due-diligence workflow"},{"type":"flow","items":["Documents","Classification","Legal Review","Financial Review","Risk Identification","Issue Categorization","Final Report"]}]},{"heading":"Projects During LL.B.","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Project 1 — Insolvency Case Database"},{"type":"p","text":"Build an Excel/Notion database containing:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Case"},{"text":"Tribunal"},{"text":"Year"},{"text":"Key issue"},{"text":"Relevant provision"},{"text":"Judgment"},{"text":"Outcome"},{"text":"Practical significance"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Project 2 — Creditor Claims Tracker"},{"type":"p","text":"Build a fictional claims-management workbook containing:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Creditor"},{"text":"Claim amount"},{"text":"Documents received"},{"text":"Verification status"},{"text":"Claim type"},{"text":"Remarks"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Project 3 — NCLT Case Analysis"},{"type":"p","text":"Select a publicly available insolvency case and prepare:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Facts"},{"text":"Parties"},{"text":"Default"},{"text":"Legal issues"},{"text":"Arguments"},{"text":"Tribunal decision"},{"text":"Appeal status"},{"text":"Practical lesson"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Project 4 — Resolution Plan Analysis"},{"type":"p","text":"Create a fictional resolution plan and analyze:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Applicant eligibility"},{"text":"Financial proposal"},{"text":"Creditor treatment"},{"text":"Implementation plan"},{"text":"Legal risks"},{"text":"Recovery implications"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Project 5 — Insolvency Timeline Dashboard"},{"type":"p","text":"Build a Power BI/Excel dashboard showing:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Case stage"},{"text":"Key deadlines"},{"text":"Hearings"},{"text":"Claims"},{"text":"Creditor status"},{"text":"Pending actions"}]}]},{"heading":"Internship Strategy","kind":"internships","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Year 1"},{"type":"p","text":"Target:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Litigation chambers"},{"text":"Corporate-law teams"},{"text":"Legal research organizations"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Goal:"},{"type":"p","text":"Build legal research fundamentals."},{"type":"h","text":"Year 2"},{"type":"p","text":"Target:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Corporate law firms"},{"text":"Banking/finance teams"},{"text":"Insolvency practices"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Goal:"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn corporate and financial law."},{"type":"h","text":"Year 3"},{"type":"p","text":"Target:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Insolvency Professional Entities"},{"text":"Resolution Professional teams"},{"text":"Restructuring practices"},{"text":"NCLT litigation teams"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Goal:"},{"type":"p","text":"Gain direct IBC exposure."},{"type":"h","text":"Final Year"},{"type":"p","text":"Target:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Insolvency/restructuring law firms"},{"text":"IP teams"},{"text":"Resolution Professional offices"},{"text":"Financial institutions"},{"text":"Restructuring consultancies"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Goal:"},{"type":"p","text":"Develop specialized insolvency experience."}]},{"heading":"Employer Skill Matrix","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Employer","Important Skills"],"rows":[[{"text":"Insolvency Professional Entity"},{"text":"IBC + Documentation + Case Management"}],[{"text":"Resolution Professional Office"},{"text":"Claims + CoC + Compliance"}],[{"text":"Law Firm"},{"text":"IBC + NCLT + Legal Research"}],[{"text":"Restructuring Consultancy"},{"text":"Finance + IBC + Due Diligence"}],[{"text":"Bank"},{"text":"Recovery + Security + Insolvency"}],[{"text":"NBFC"},{"text":"Debt + Recovery + Compliance"}],[{"text":"Corporate Legal Team"},{"text":"Restructuring + Contracts"}],[{"text":"Investment Firm"},{"text":"Distressed Assets + Due Diligence"}],[{"text":"Financial Consultancy"},{"text":"Valuation + Restructuring"}],[{"text":"Insolvency Litigation Practice"},{"text":"IBC + Procedure + Advocacy"}]]}]},{"heading":"Legal Research Resources","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Develop strong research skills using:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"SCC Online"},{"text":"Manupatra"},{"text":"LexisNexis"},{"text":"Westlaw"},{"text":"Indian Kanoon"},{"text":"Official IBBI resources"},{"text":"NCLT/NCLAT decisions"},{"text":"Government legal resources"}]},{"type":"p","text":"For insolvency work, always verify the current version of the IBC, IBBI regulations, notifications, circulars and relevant judicial decisions."}]},{"heading":"AI & Insolvency","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"AI can assist insolvency teams with:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Case-document summarization"},{"text":"Contract review"},{"text":"Case chronology"},{"text":"Document classification"},{"text":"Claims-document organization"},{"text":"Legal research"},{"text":"Resolution-plan comparison"},{"text":"Data extraction"},{"text":"Compliance tracking"}]},{"type":"h","text":"AI-assisted workflow"},{"type":"flow","items":["Large Case File","AI Document Classification","Human Verification","Claims / Contract / Evidence Mapping","Legal Research","Risk Analysis","Final Professional Review"]},{"type":"p","text":"AI should not independently determine creditor claims, legal rights or statutory compliance without qualified human review."}]},{"heading":"Certifications & Additional Learning","kind":"certifications","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Useful areas:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Insolvency & Bankruptcy Law"},{"text":"Corporate Restructuring"},{"text":"Corporate Law"},{"text":"Banking & Finance Law"},{"text":"Debt Recovery"},{"text":"Contract Drafting"},{"text":"Legal Research"},{"text":"Financial Analysis"},{"text":"Valuation Fundamentals"},{"text":"Negotiation"},{"text":"Arbitration"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Professional pathway"},{"type":"p","text":"Students interested in eventually becoming an Insolvency Professional should separately study the current IBBI eligibility, examination, experience and registration requirements rather than assuming that an LL.B. alone provides eligibility."}]},{"heading":"PG Options","kind":"pg_india","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"LL.M."},{"type":"p","text":"Relevant choices:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"LL.M. in Insolvency & Bankruptcy Law"},{"text":"LL.M. in Corporate Law"},{"text":"LL.M. in Corporate & Commercial Law"},{"text":"LL.M. in Banking & Finance Law"},{"text":"LL.M. in Business Law"},{"text":"LL.M. in Commercial Law"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Other Options"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"PG Diploma in Insolvency & Bankruptcy Law"},{"text":"Corporate restructuring programs"},{"text":"Financial restructuring courses"},{"text":"Valuation programs"},{"text":"MBA Finance"}]},{"type":"flow","items":["A combination of law","finance","restructuring is particularly valuable."],"sep":"+"}]},{"heading":"Career Specializations","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Insolvency Litigation"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"IBC litigation"},{"text":"NCLT"},{"text":"NCLAT"},{"text":"Judicial interpretation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Corporate Restructuring"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Debt restructuring"},{"text":"Corporate reorganization"},{"text":"Distressed companies"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Claims Management"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Creditor claims"},{"text":"Verification"},{"text":"Documentation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Resolution Planning"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Resolution applicants"},{"text":"Resolution plans"},{"text":"Commercial and legal analysis"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Liquidation"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Asset realization"},{"text":"Creditor claims"},{"text":"Distribution"},{"text":"Liquidation processes"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Distressed Asset Advisory"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Financial analysis"},{"text":"Valuation"},{"text":"Debt recovery"},{"text":"Investment opportunities"}]}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"0–2 Years"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Legal Intern"},{"text":"Insolvency Intern"},{"text":"Legal Executive"},{"text":"Insolvency Associate"},{"text":"Resolution Professional Assistant"}]},{"type":"h","text":"2–5 Years"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Senior Insolvency Associate"},{"text":"Restructuring Associate"},{"text":"Insolvency Legal Associate"},{"text":"Resolution Professional Team Lead"}]},{"type":"h","text":"5–10 Years"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Insolvency Specialist"},{"text":"Restructuring Counsel"},{"text":"Senior Legal Counsel"},{"text":"Insolvency Advisory Manager"}]},{"type":"h","text":"10+ Years"},{"type":"p","text":"Potential directions include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Insolvency Professional pathway, subject to statutory eligibility"},{"text":"Restructuring Consultant"},{"text":"Insolvency Legal Specialist"},{"text":"Insolvency Advisory Head"},{"text":"Partner in an insolvency/restructuring practice"}]}]},{"heading":"Emerging Opportunities","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Emerging Area","Opportunity"],"rows":[[{"text":"AI"},{"text":"Insolvency document analysis"}],[{"text":"RegTech"},{"text":"Regulatory compliance"}],[{"text":"FinTech"},{"text":"Digital lending distress"}],[{"text":"Data Analytics"},{"text":"Creditor/claims analysis"}],[{"text":"Distressed Investing"},{"text":"Asset and restructuring analysis"}],[{"text":"Legal Tech"},{"text":"Automated document review"}],[{"text":"Cross-Border Insolvency"},{"text":"International restructuring"}],[{"text":"ESG"},{"text":"Distress and sustainability risk"}],[{"text":"Cybersecurity"},{"text":"Insolvency data protection"}],[{"text":"Digital Assets"},{"text":"Emerging insolvency questions"}]]}]},{"heading":"Target Profile at Graduation","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A strong candidate should demonstrate:"},{"type":"h","text":"Legal"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Insolvency & Bankruptcy Law"},{"text":"Company Law"},{"text":"Contract Law"},{"text":"Banking & Finance Law"},{"text":"Civil Procedure"},{"text":"Evidence"},{"text":"NCLT/NCLAT procedure"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Financial"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Financial statements"},{"text":"Debt"},{"text":"Security"},{"text":"Recovery"},{"text":"Valuation basics"},{"text":"Restructuring concepts"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Practical"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Claims analysis"},{"text":"Legal research"},{"text":"Case summaries"},{"text":"Due diligence"},{"text":"Resolution-plan analysis"},{"text":"Compliance tracking"},{"text":"Documentation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Portfolio"},{"type":"p","text":"Ideally:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"2+ insolvency internships"},{"text":"10+ case briefs"},{"text":"1 creditor claims tracker"},{"text":"1 resolution-plan analysis"},{"text":"1 NCLT case study"},{"text":"1 insolvency dashboard"},{"text":"1 restructuring research paper"}]}]},{"heading":"Recommended Final Skill Stack","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"LL.B."},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"IBC / Insolvency Law"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Company Law"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Banking & Finance Law"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"NCLT / NCLAT Knowledge"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Claims Management"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Resolution Planning"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Corporate Restructuring"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Legal Research"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Due Diligence"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Financial Statement Analysis"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Excel / Power BI"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Legal Technology"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"AI-Assisted Document Analysis"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Relevant Insolvency Internship"}]},{"heading":"Best Overall Positioning","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"The strongest profile for a Resolution Professional Assistant is:"},{"type":"flow","items":["LL.B.","Insolvency & Bankruptcy Law","Company Law","Banking & Finance","NCLT/NCLAT Knowledge","Claims Management","Resolution Planning","Financial Analysis","Due Diligence","Excel/Power BI","Insolvency Internship"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"The key differentiator is combining legal knowledge with financial and process-management skills. A strong candidate should understand not only what the IBC says, but also how a real insolvency assignment is managed—from claims and creditor records to CoC meetings, resolution-plan analysis, documentation, regulatory timelines and tribunal proceedings."}]}]}